1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,750
This is the Submission Triage Desk, a concept extension of Heron for a fictional funder.

2
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:10,120
Twelve broker submissions sit in the shared inbox, each with its ask, completeness and a live SLA clock.

3
00:00:10,822 --> 00:00:12,398
I open Bluewave Auto Detailing.

4
00:00:12,398 --> 00:00:18,042
Before anyone touched it, every attachment was classified, with a confidence score and a one-click reclassify.

5
00:00:18,761 --> 00:00:21,197
Every extracted number carries an evidence chip.

6
00:00:21,197 --> 00:00:24,851
Tap one, and the source statement opens on the exact line it came from.

7
00:00:25,564 --> 00:00:28,185
The scrub engine re-adds every running balance.

8
00:00:28,185 --> 00:00:30,248
One printed balance does not follow.

9
00:00:30,248 --> 00:00:33,147
The rule is shown, and the flag waits for a person.

10
00:00:33,147 --> 00:00:34,764
I confirm it, with a reason.

11
00:00:35,479 --> 00:00:40,014
The funder's credit policy runs as explicit rules, pass or fail, with the reason.

12
00:00:40,014 --> 00:00:41,749
Passing never approves a deal.

13
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:48,056
With every flag reviewed, I choose an outcome, write the rationale, and export a CRM-ready package.

14
00:00:48,056 --> 00:00:50,148
Every step lands in the audit trail.

15
00:00:50,853 --> 00:00:54,183
The eval lab scores the engine on twenty-four seeded submissions.

16
00:00:54,183 --> 00:00:57,103
Eighteen of nineteen defects caught, one false positive.

17
00:00:57,805 --> 00:01:01,746
And here is the honest miss: a re-typed statement with consistent balances.

18
00:01:01,746 --> 00:01:03,795
Catching that needs bank-sourced data.

19
00:01:04,506 --> 00:01:05,974
Submission Triage Desk.

20
00:01:05,974 --> 00:01:08,143
Independent concept by Ayo Ahmed.

21
00:01:08,143 --> 00:01:09,866
Not affiliated with Heron.
